WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.920
Hypothermic intraperitoneal
chemotherapy, or HIPEC,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.020
is a treatment option for
patients with advanced cancers

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.630
that have spread to the
abdominal cavity or peritoneum.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.000
Doctors begin with what is
called cytoreductive surgery

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.100
to remove all visible tumors
in the abdominal area.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.710
The extent of the surgery
depends on the findings

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.420
during surgery.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.860
Surgery can involve
the removal of tumors

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:54.500
in the upper and lower
abdominal area on the omentum,

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:09.120
on the liver, stomach, small
intestine, colon, rectum,

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:20.490
pancreas, spleen,
appendix, uterus,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:27.700
ovaries, and the
peritoneal surfaces.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.850
Surgery to remove tumors
is thorough and aggressive

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:37.500
with the goal of preserving
organs whenever possible.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.120
The doctor carefully examines
the abdominal region,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.410
quadrant by quadrant, searching
for and removing tumors.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.430
With great care, the
doctor uses highly

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:53.500
specialized surgical
techniques to strip the tumors

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.890
from the peritoneal
surfaces and organs

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:59.300
and seal small blood vessels.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:05.000
All of the visible
tumors are removed.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.570
Next, the doctor administers
the HIPEC or heated chemotherapy

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.420
treatment, with a goal of
killing any remaining cancer

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.900
cells that cannot be seen.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.960
Tubes and temperature
probes are placed

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:24.100
into the abdominal cavity.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.070
The doctor briefly
closes the skin

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.300
of the abdomen with sutures.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.090
The abdominal cavity is
flooded with a solution

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.350
that includes
chemotherapy drugs.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:38.600
This solution is heated.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:42.670
The tubes and probes are
connected to a machine.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:47.500
This controls the temperature
and flow of the solution.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.350
The heated chemotherapy
solution is continuously

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.740
circulated throughout
the abdominal cavity

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.290
so that the cavity
is uniformly exposed

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.300
to heat and chemotherapy.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.830
The combination of
heat and chemotherapy

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:08.100
causes the solution to kill
microscopic cancer cells.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:11.990
Gentle shaking is
applied to the abdomen

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:14.930
to help the solution
distribute to all surfaces

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.580
within the abdomen.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.810
Following the HIPEC
treatment, the fluid

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:23.500
is drained from the
abdominal cavity.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:29.710
The abdomen is reopened and the
tubes and probes are removed.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.850
At this time, any necessary
reconstructive surgery

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.170
is performed.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:39.600
For example, the doctor may need
to reconnect a resected colon.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.800
Finally the doctor closes
the abdominal incision.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.150
The surgery and HIPEC
treatment together

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:49.222
may take 6 to 12
hours to complete.

